 /tmp tied to timesyncd) are normal, expected byproducts of a genuine reboot rather than executor residue. No failed services or listening-socket changes were introduced, and dpkg package health remained consistent across before/after snapshots.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"cmd-3102d0029f004b68\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"Both material outcomes—blocking usb_storage from loading immediately and after reboot—are directly and coherently demonstrated. The executor established a healthy baseline, applied a standard blacklist + install /bin/false override, regenerated initramfs, and then performed and verified an actual reboot (confirmed by independent boot-identity cross-check) followed by re-verification that the block persisted. No unnecessary or risky mutations were found.\",\"limitations\":[\"Post-reboot verification relies on lsmod/modprobe checks rather than direct inspection of which specific initramfs image was booted, though the embedded-config check pre-reboot plus the confirmed boot-identity change and post-reboot re-verification make this a minor gap.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"block-now","requirement":"usb-storage module is blocked from loading immediately on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline (cmd-cf60b70841d34d82) showed usb_storage could be inserted via modprobe. After writing /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist-usb-storage.conf with 'blacklist usb_storage' and 'install usb_storage /bin/false' (cmd-762e1ae5b75041f6), a modprobe dry-run showed the install override and an actual modprobe attempt failed with 'Operation not permitted', with the module absent from lsmod (cmd-41bda4306ae84441).","evidence_ids":["cmd-cf60b70841d34d82","cmd-762e1ae5b75041f6","cmd-41bda4306ae84441"]},{"id":"block-after-reboot","requirement":"usb-storage module remains blocked from loading after a reboot","status":"satisfied"